+    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
+    // KNOWN FAILURES — real bugs found by the round-trip properties above.
+    // These pin the bugs deterministically and are expected to FAIL until
+    // the bugs are fixed. Do not "fix" the tests. See HEGEL_REPORT.md.
+    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+    /// KNOWN FAILURE (real bug): `Gamma::inverse_cdf` (and `ChiSquared` /
+    /// `Erlang`, which delegate to it) is catastrophically wrong whenever the
+    /// true quantile is smaller than ~1e-9. The safeguarded Newton loop in
+    /// `Gamma::inverse_cdf` stops via `prec::convergence`, which accepts a
+    /// step below `DEFAULT_EPS = 1e-9` *absolute*; when the search bisects
+    /// down toward a tiny quantile the steps shrink below 1e-9 long before
+    /// reaching it. Here the true median of Gamma(1e-3, 1) is ~1e-301, but
+    /// inverse_cdf(0.5) returns ~9.3e-10, whose cdf is ~0.98.
+    #[test]
